{
  "_doc": [
    "Estimated per-link masses (kg) for SourcceyMkV.urdf. The CAD export gives every part the density of steel (169 kg in total); a printed Sourccey is about a tenth of that.",
    "NOT weighed. Printed PLA+ parts: 1.23 g/cm3, 10 % infill, shell thickness calibrated so the robot totals 15.9 kg (the published 'just under 16 kg'). Bought parts and electronics from datasheets / retail listings: 12 Feetech servos by joint type (STS3250 on shoulder_lift and elbow_flex, STS3215 elsewhere), 100 mm mecanum wheels 0.34 kg, 37 mm gearmotors 0.20 kg, linear actuator 1.5 kg (assumed 12 V ~300 mm), 4S LiFePO4 pack 1.55 kg (assumed), Raspberry Pi 5 + cooler, PCB and drivers, rear screen 0.30 kg (assumed), cameras, LD19 LiDAR; electronics that are not in the CAD are added to the link they mount on; 0.6 kg of wiring and fasteners spread over printed parts.",
    "sourccey/build.py scales each link's inertia tensor by the same ratio, so the centre of mass and the shape of the inertia are the CAD's. Replace any entry with a weighed value; `python -m sourccey.build --cad-masses` keeps the CAD masses."
